HELP SYSTEM_SERVICE $system-service-you-want
gives you everything you need including the C prototypes.

The big thing is descriptors.  Strings are passed by descriptors,
not as CHAR*.

#include <descrip.h>

You should look at the DESCRIP.H file.

If you really know C, this is all the info you need to do what you want to
do.

There is also VMS documentation on CDROM which the people you
are working for should have if they are doing VMS software development.

I think some people have it spinning on the internet for perusal using a
browser.

Just my opinion,


Rick...


