 The best source of information about system services is the
"System Services Reference Manual" which is in the programming
section of the OpenVMS documentation set.

You may also be interested in the book,
"Practical Uses of OpenVMS System Services
  --  Emulating DCL in FORTRAN and C Programs"
It has a chapter explaining how to call system services in FORTRAN
and C.  It has 70 examples in each language that demonstrate
several system services and show how to perform the same
functions as common DCL commands.

See our web page for details.

Retha Taylor
